As such, we introduce…]]></description><link>https://string.eusa.ed.ac.uk//2020-07-06-positive-notes/</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://string.eusa.ed.ac.uk//2020-07-06-positive-notes/</guid><category><![CDATA[covid]]></category><category><![CDATA[positive notes]]></category><category><![CDATA[euso]]></category><category><![CDATA[edinburgh university string orchestra]]></category><category><![CDATA[edinburgh]]></category><category><![CDATA[university of edinburgh]]></category><pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2020 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;In light of the coronavirus outbreak and the impact on daily life and mental health, we thought it would be worth sharing some music which brings us comfort.
As such, we introduce our &lt;code class=&quot;language-text&quot;&gt;#positivenotes&lt;/code&gt; campaign!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We will be asking our members to share short clips of them playing music that uplifts them or brings them comfort in the hope that others will feel the same.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/edinstrings/&quot;&gt;Instagram account&lt;/a&gt; to watch the first few instalments!&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded><author>euso.president@gmail.com</author></item></channel></rss>